<title>UK: UK minister to make substantive beef ban statement.</title>
<headline>UK minister to make substantive beef ban statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Minister Jack Cunningham is to give details later on Tuesday of government plans to get the European Union ban on exports of British beef lifted, government sources said.</p>
<p>They said Cunningham would give a substantive written answer to a question put down on Tuesday's parliamentary order paper by fellow Labour MP Russell Brown, the member for the Scottish constituency of Dumfries.</p>
<p>Brown has asked Cunningham &quot;what plans he has for a new initiative to secure the lifting of the beef export ban&quot;.</p>
<p>The EU has banned exports of British beef worldwide since March last year following scientific evidence that people eating beef from cows infected with &quot;mad cow disease&quot; risk developing the human version of the brain-wasting malady. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
